 "text": "Hi! How are you doing these days? To get neutral skin, start with a very light layer and build up slowly. Start in the middle and then edge towards the high points. Exactly. A light green works well, and it cancels the orange. Use shades of brown for darker skin, and mix in just little of a light green for tans. Too much green makes it glowy, so go slow. I wouldn't. Mix small amount, maybe a tablespoon at most, and use it up quickly. A bit of brown mixed with your skin shade in very small amounts can help. Starting in the skin shadows on sides and top helps too.",
